WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.500
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:03.660
STANLEY Y SHAW: Every day,
millions of data points

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.850
are being generated about your health.

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.590
What if all this data could be combined
and shared with health care teams

00:00:10.590 --> 00:00:12.540
to improve patient care?

00:00:12.540 --> 00:00:17.400
The reality is that health care is
very different from retail or banking

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:18.810
or travel.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.940
And digital transformation in health
care need people who are bilingual,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.700
fluent in the powerful
new digital tools that

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:32.270
are emerging, but also in the culture
and workflows of real-life medicine.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.320
We have to take a health
care-centered view of tech disruption.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:40.250
In digital health, you explore
the opportunities and caveats

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:44.520
related to the widespread adoption
of digital tools in health care.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:49.370
You'll acquire new frameworks to
help you navigate stakeholder needs,

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:53.600
create value, foster
trust and engagement,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:57.860
demonstrate improved outcomes,
and develop sustainable business

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:03.830
models, and all of this in the unique
context of the health care ecosystem.

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:06.515
SEAN DUFFY: I really think
we're the first inning of what's

00:01:06.515 --> 00:01:07.640
possible in digital health.

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:10.760
And we'll go on a journey
over the next decade, where

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:13.670
more and more and more
of clinical services

00:01:13.670 --> 00:01:16.850
will be pushed either into the pocket,
into the home, or into the cloud.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:19.600
KATHERINE CHOU: But ultimately,
people are expecting for that data

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:22.628
to be used for the purposes of
improving their health care outcomes.

00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:24.920
MARCUS OSBORNE: The most
important thing that we can do

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:28.070
is how we can create a path
forward to leverage data

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:31.250
to really help people
get insights that can

00:01:31.250 --> 00:01:34.220
help them better engage
in their health and better

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:35.860
understand what's going on right now.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:37.610
STANLEY Y SHAW: This
program is for anyone

00:01:37.610 --> 00:01:41.510
who wants to learn more about leading
digital-enabled initiatives in health

00:01:41.510 --> 00:01:42.200
care.

00:01:42.200 --> 00:01:44.730
The future of health care is digital.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:47.480
[MUSIC PLAYING]

